The first generator did exactly what it needed to do: it created a combinatorial playground where the rules were deliberately thin enough for unexpected interpretations to emerge.

What happened afterward was useful. By trying to reason through particles, stress, rotation, coupling, curvature, and HH pairings, we exposed which meanings were stable, which were ambiguous, and which ambiguities were productive.

So the next version is not a correction. It is an **expansion of the game**.

Version one generated:

